9. OBSTACLE FAIRNESS & COLLISION VALIDATION

Gameplay difficulty must come from skill, not unfair random generation.

Every generated obstacle pattern must be validated.

Never generate:

- All three lanes blocked simultaneously without a viable solution.
- Impossible obstacle combinations.
- Obstacles appearing directly on the player.
- Insufficient reaction time.
- Unavoidable collision sequences.
- Jump obstacles that cannot be cleared.
- Slides that begin too late.
- Incorrect collision boxes.
- Obstacles that visually appear avoidable but are not.

Calculate obstacle spacing based on:

- Current player speed.
- Player reaction time.
- Lane-switch duration.
- Jump duration.
- Slide duration.
- Obstacle collision dimensions.
- Track geometry.

Every obstacle pattern must have at least one mathematically valid solution.

The player must be able to react fairly.

